        "subject": "LU-21276 tests: fix sanityn/39 clock skew checks",
        "message": "LU-21276 tests: fix sanityn/39 clock skew checks\n\nFix sanityn test_39a and test_39d to account for minor skew between\nkernel and userspace clocks.  This extends the sanity.sh fix in\n\"LU-12105 tests: fix sanity/39 checks and style\" to sanityn.sh,\nwhich has the same problem but was not touched by that patch.\n\nBoth tests bracket a write with userspace \"date +%s\" reads and then\nrequire d1 <= mtime <= d2.  When the kernel timestamp recorded for\nthe write falls just outside that window, the check fails even\nthough mtime was updated correctly, so sleep briefly on either side\nof the write to widen the window.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=\"39a 39d\",ONLY_REPEAT=20\nSigned-off-by: John Grasso <johgras@amazon.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I256ed40b07a9d82ef7871f647cc5258d4d232167\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
